#: ../../reference/glossary/device-software.rst:10
msgid "Device software glossary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/device-software.rst:12
msgid ""
"This section provides brief definitions of software abstractions and "
"programming models that run on AMD GPUs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/device-software.rst:23
msgid "AMDGPU assembly"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/device-software.rst:25
msgid ""
"AMDGPU assembly (GFX ISA) is the low-level assembly format for programs "
"running on AMD GPUs, generated by the :term:`ROCm compiler toolchain <HIP"
" compiler>`. See :ref:`hip:amdgpu_assembly` for instruction set details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/device-software.rst:29
msgid "AMDGPU intermediate representation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/device-software.rst:31
msgid ""
"AMDGPU IR is an intermediate representation for GPU code, serving as a "
"virtual instruction set between high-level languages and :term"
":`architecture-specific assembly <AMDGPU assembly>`. See "
":ref:`hip:amdgpu_ir` for compilation details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/device-software.rst:69
msgid "Global memory"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/device-software.rst:71
msgid ""
"Global memory is the :term:`device-wide memory <GPU RAM (VRAM)>` "
"accessible to all :term:`threads <Work-item (Thread)>`, physically "
"implemented as HBM or GDDR. See :ref:`hip:memory_hierarchy` for global "
"memory details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/device-software.rst:42
msgid "Grid"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/device-software.rst:44
msgid ""
"A grid represents the collection of all :term:`work-groups <Work-group "
"(Block)>` executing a single :term:`kernel <HIP kernel>` across the "
"entire GPU. See :ref:`hip:inherent_thread_hierarchy_grid` for grid "
"execution details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/device-software.rst:48
msgid "HIP kernel"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/device-software.rst:50
msgid ""
"A HIP kernel is the unit of GPU code that executes in parallel across "
"many :term:`threads <Work-item (Thread)>`, distributed across the GPU's "
":term:`compute units <Compute units>`. See :ref:`hip:device_program` for "
"kernel programming details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/device-software.rst:62
msgid "HIP memory hierarchy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/device-software.rst:64
msgid ""
"The memory hierarchy pairs each :term:`thread hierarchy <HIP thread "
"hierarchy>` level with corresponding memory scopes, from :term:`private "
"registers <Register>` to :term:`LDS <Local data share>` to :term:`GPU RAM"
" <GPU RAM (VRAM)>`. See :ref:`hip:memory_hierarchy` for memory "
"architecture details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/device-software.rst:54
msgid "HIP thread hierarchy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/device-software.rst:56
msgid ""
"The thread hierarchy structures parallel work from individual "
":term:`threads <Work-item (Thread)>` to :term:`blocks <Work-group "
"(Block)>` to :term:`grids <Grid>`, mapping onto hardware from :term:`SIMD"
" lanes <SIMD core>` to :term:`compute units <Compute units>` to the "
"entire GPU. See :ref:`hip:inherent_thread_model` for complete details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/device-software.rst:35
#: ../../reference/gpu-arch-specs.rst:29 ../../reference/gpu-arch-specs.rst:308
#: ../../reference/gpu-arch-specs.rst:568
#: ../../reference/gpu-arch-specs.rst:1026
msgid "LLVM target name"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/device-software.rst:37
msgid ""
"The LLVM target name is a string identifier corresponding to a specific "
":term:`GFX IP <GFX IP>` version that is passed to the :term:`HIP compiler"
" <HIP compiler>` toolchain to specify the target GPU architecture for "
"code generation. See :doc:`llvm-project:reference/rocmcc` for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/device-software.rst:17
msgid "ROCm programming model"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/device-software.rst:19
msgid ""
"The ROCm programming model defines how AMD GPUs execute massively "
"parallel programs using hierarchical :term:`work-groups <Work-group "
"(Block)>`, memory scopes, and barrier synchronization. See "
":ref:`hip:programming_model` for complete details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/host-software.rst:-1
msgid "Host software glossary for AMD GPUs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/host-software.rst:-1
msgid ""
"AMD, ROCm, GPU, host software, HIP, compiler, runtime, libraries, "
"profiler, amd-smi"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/host-software.rst:10
msgid "Host software glossary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/host-software.rst:12
msgid ""
"This section provides brief definitions of development tools, compilers, "
"libraries, and runtime environments for programming AMD GPUs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/host-software.rst:30
msgid "AMD SMI"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/host-software.rst:32
msgid ""
"The ``amd-smi`` command-line utility queries, monitors, and manages AMD "
"GPU state, providing hardware information and performance metrics. See "
":doc:`amdsmi:index` for detailed usage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/host-software.rst:23
msgid "HIP C++ language extension"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/host-software.rst:25
msgid ""
"HIP extends the C++ language with additional features designed for "
"programming heterogeneous applications. These extensions mostly relate to"
" the kernel language, but some can also be applied to host functionality."
" See :doc:`hip:how-to/hip_cpp_language_extensions` for language "
"fundamentals."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/host-software.rst:40
msgid "HIP compiler"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/host-software.rst:42
msgid ""
"The HIP compiler ``amdclang++`` compiles HIP C++ programs into binaries "
"that contain both host CPU and device GPU code. See :doc:`llvm-"
"project:reference/rocmcc` for compiler flags and options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/host-software.rst:35
msgid "HIP runtime API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/host-software.rst:37
msgid ""
"The HIP runtime API provides an interface for GPU programming, offering "
"functions for memory management, kernel launches, and synchronization. "
"See :ref:`hip:hip_runtime_api_how-to` for API overview."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/host-software.rst:45
msgid "HIP runtime compiler"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/host-software.rst:47
msgid ""
"The HIP Runtime Compiler (HIPRTC) compiles HIP source code at runtime "
"into :term:`AMDGPU <AMDGPU assembly>` binary code objects, enabling just-"
"in-time kernel generation, device-specific optimization, and dynamic code"
" creation for different GPUs. See :ref:`hip:hip_runtime_compiler_how-to` "
"for API details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/host-software.rst:52
msgid "ROCgdb"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/host-software.rst:54
msgid ""
"ROCgdb is AMD's source-level debugger for HIP and ROCm applications, "
"enabling debugging of both host CPU and GPU device code, including kernel"
" breakpoints, stepping, and variable inspection. See :doc:`rocgdb:index` "
"for usage and command reference."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/host-software.rst:63
msgid "ROCm and LLVM binary utilities"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/host-software.rst:65
msgid ""
"ROCm and LLVM binary utilities are command-line tools for examining and "
"manipulating GPU binaries and code objects. See "
":ref:`hip:binary_utilities` for utility details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/host-software.rst:17
msgid "ROCm software platform"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/host-software.rst:19
msgid ""
"ROCm is AMD's GPU software stack, providing compiler toolchains, runtime "
"environments, and performance libraries for HPC and AI applications. See "
":doc:`../../what-is-rocm` for a complete component overview."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/host-software.rst:58
msgid "rocprofv3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/host-software.rst:60
msgid ""
"``rocprofv3`` is AMD's primary performance analysis tool, providing "
"profiling, tracing, and performance counter collection. See :ref"
":`rocprofiler-sdk:using-rocprofv3` for profiling workflows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/performance.rst:-1
msgid "Performance glossary for AMD GPUs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/performance.rst:-1
msgid ""
"AMD, ROCm, GPU, performance, optimization, roofline, bottleneck, "
"occupancy, bandwidth, latency hiding, divergence"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/performance.rst:10
msgid "Performance analysis glossary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/performance.rst:12
msgid ""
"This section provides brief definitions of performance analysis concepts "
"and optimization techniques."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/performance.rst:73
msgid "Active cycle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/performance.rst:75
msgid ""
"An active cycle is a clock cycle in which a :term:`compute unit <Compute "
"units>` has at least one active :term:`wavefront <Wavefront>` resident. "
"See :ref:`hip:wavefront_execution` for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/performance.rst:57
msgid "Arithmetic bandwidth"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/performance.rst:59
msgid ""
"Arithmetic bandwidth is the peak rate at which arithmetic work can be "
"performed, defining the compute roof in :term:`roofline models <Roofline "
"model>`. See :ref:`hip:compute_bound` for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/performance.rst:37
msgid "Arithmetic intensity"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/performance.rst:39
msgid ""
"Arithmetic intensity is the ratio of arithmetic operations to memory "
"operations in a kernel, and determines performance characteristics. See "
":ref:`hip:arithmetic_intensity` for intensity analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/performance.rst:124
msgid "Bank conflict"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/performance.rst:126
msgid ""
"A bank conflict occurs when multiple threads simultaneously access "
"different addresses in the same :term:`LDS bank <Local data share>`, "
"serializing accesses. See :ref:`hip:bank_conflicts_theory` for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/performance.rst:112
msgid "Branch efficiency"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/performance.rst:114
msgid ""
"Branch efficiency measures how often all threads within a "
":term:`wavefront <Wavefront>` take the same execution path, quantifying "
"control-flow uniformity. See :ref:`hip:branch_efficiency` for branch "
"analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/performance.rst:23
msgid "Compute-bound"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/performance.rst:25
msgid ""
"Compute-bound kernels are limited by the :term:`arithmetic bandwidth "
"<Arithmetic bandwidth>` of the GPU's :term:`compute units <Compute "
"units>` rather than :term:`memory bandwidth <Memory bandwidth>`. See "
":ref:`hip:compute_bound` for compute-bound analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/performance.rst:101
msgid "CU utilization"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/performance.rst:103
msgid ""
"CU utilization measures the percentage of time that :term:`compute units "
"<Compute units>` are actively executing instructions. See "
":ref:`hip:cu_utilization` for utilization analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/performance.rst:95
msgid "Issue efficiency"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/performance.rst:97
msgid ""
"Issue efficiency measures how effectively the :term:`wavefront scheduler "
"<Wavefront scheduler>` keeps execution pipelines busy by issuing "
"instructions. See :ref:`hip:issue_efficiency` for efficiency metrics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/performance.rst:63
msgid "Latency hiding"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/performance.rst:65
msgid ""
"Latency hiding masks long-latency operations by running many concurrent "
"threads, keeping execution pipelines busy. See :ref:`hip:latency_hiding` "
"for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/performance.rst:47
msgid "Little's Law"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/performance.rst:49
msgid ""
"Little's Law relates concurrency, latency, and throughput, determining "
"how much independent work must be in flight to hide latency. See "
":ref:`hip:littles_law` for latency hiding details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/performance.rst:52
msgid "Memory bandwidth"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/performance.rst:54
msgid ""
"Memory bandwidth is the maximum rate at which data can be transferred "
"between memory hierarchy levels, typically measured in bytes per second. "
"See :ref:`hip:memory_bound` for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/performance.rst:118
msgid "Memory coalescing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/performance.rst:120
msgid ""
"Memory coalescing improves :term:`memory bandwidth <Memory bandwidth>` by"
" servicing many logical loads or stores with fewer physical memory "
"transactions. See :ref:`hip:memory_coalescing_theory` for coalescing "
"patterns."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/performance.rst:30
msgid "Memory-bound"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/performance.rst:32
msgid ""
"Memory-bound kernels are limited by :term:`memory bandwidth <Memory "
"bandwidth>` rather than :term:`arithmetic bandwidth <Arithmetic "
"bandwidth>`, typically due to low :term:`arithmetic intensity <Arithmetic"
" intensity>`. See :ref:`hip:memory_bound` for memory-bound analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/performance.rst:79
msgid "Occupancy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/performance.rst:81
msgid ""
"Occupancy is the ratio of active :term:`wavefronts <Wavefront>` to the "
"maximum number of wavefronts that can be active on a :term:`compute unit "
"<Compute units>`. See :ref:`hip:occupancy` for occupancy analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/performance.rst:42
msgid "Overhead"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/performance.rst:44
msgid ""
"Overhead latency is the time spent with no useful work being done, often "
"due to CPU-side bottlenecks or kernel launch delays. See "
":ref:`hip:performance_bottlenecks` for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/performance.rst:90
msgid "Peak rate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/performance.rst:92
msgid ""
"Peak rate is the theoretical maximum throughput at which a hardware "
"system can complete work under ideal conditions. See "
":ref:`hip:theoretical_performance_limits` for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/performance.rst:85
msgid "Pipe utilization"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/performance.rst:87
msgid ""
"Pipe utilization measures how effectively a kernel uses the execution "
"pipelines within each :term:`compute unit <Compute units>`. See "
":ref:`hip:pipe_utilization` for utilization details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/performance.rst:129
msgid "Register pressure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/performance.rst:131
msgid ""
"Register pressure occurs when excessive register demand limits the number"
" of active :term:`wavefronts <Wavefront>` per :term:`compute unit "
"<Compute units>`, reducing :term:`occupancy <Occupancy>`. See "
":ref:`hip:register_pressure_theory` for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/performance.rst:17
msgid "Roofline model"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/performance.rst:19
msgid ""
"The roofline model is a visual performance model that determines whether "
"a program is :term:`compute-bound <Compute-bound>` or :term:`memory-bound"
" <Memory-bound>`. See :ref:`hip:roofline_model` for roofline analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/performance.rst:106
msgid "Wavefront divergence"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/performance.rst:108
msgid ""
"Wavefront divergence occurs when threads within a :term:`wavefront "
"<Wavefront>` take different execution paths due to conditional "
"statements. See :ref:`hip:branch_efficiency` for divergence handling "
"details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/performance.rst:68
msgid "Wavefront execution state"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/glossary/performance.rst:70
msgid ""
"Wavefront execution states (*active*, *stalled*, *eligible*, *selected*) "
"describe the scheduling status of :term:`wavefronts <Wavefront>` on AMD "
"GPUs. See :ref:`hip:wavefront_execution` for state definitions."
msgstr ""

