#: ../../reference/gpu-atomics-operation.rst:222
msgid ""
"Hardware atomics support refers to the ability of GPUs to natively "
"perform atomic operations—special low-level operations that ensure data "
"consistency when multiple threads access and modify memory concurrently."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/gpu-atomics-operation.rst:226
msgid ""
"CAS (Compare-and-Swap) atomic support refers to the hardware or software "
"capability to perform an atomic Compare-and-Swap operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/gpu-atomics-operation.rst:229
msgid ""
"PCIe atomics are a feature of the PCIe interface that enable atomic "
"operations between devices and hosts across the PCIe bus. For further "
"information, please check `How ROCm uses PCIe atomics "
"<https://instinct.docs.amd.com/projects/amdgpu-docs/en/latest/conceptual"
"/pcie-atomics.html>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/gpu-atomics-operation.rst:233
msgid ""
"The tables that follow show the correctness of atomics operations on the "
"hardware using the following notations:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/gpu-atomics-operation.rst:236
msgid "✅: Produces the correct answer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/gpu-atomics-operation.rst:238
msgid "⚠️: Produces the correct answer, but works only at a weaker scope."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/gpu-atomics-operation.rst:240
msgid "❌: The atomics operation fails."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/gpu-atomics-operation.rst:242
msgid ""
"The tables show the different types of atomic operations used by specific"
" devices:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/gpu-atomics-operation.rst:245
msgid ""
"Native: Computes the correct result using a hardware-native atomic "
"instruction."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/gpu-atomics-operation.rst:248
msgid ""
"CAS: Generates the correct result, but the atomic operation is "
"implemented by the compiler for this ISA using a compare-and-swap "
"emulation loop."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/gpu-atomics-operation.rst:251
msgid ""
"✅ NoReturn: Produces the correct correct result but does not precisely "
"conform to the atomic API."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/gpu-atomics-operation.rst:254
msgid ""
"Scope Downgrade: Generates the correct result but operates at a weaker "
"scope than requested. For example, if a user specifies a system-scope "
"atomic, the operation may only function at the device scope."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/gpu-atomics-operation.rst:258
msgid ""
"NOP: The atomic operation is not executed on the target location, and the"
" requesting thread receives back 0 as a return value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/gpu-atomics-operation.rst:261
msgid ""
"n/a: The atomic type is not supported and cannot be executed on the "
"specific hardware."
msgstr ""

